<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Army of the Holy Faith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1799">1799</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sanfedisti</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Army of the Holy Faith (Sanfedisti) was the peasant army raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> in 1799 by Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fabrizio-ruffo">Fabrizio Ruffo</a> to restore the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> king Ferdinand IV. Marching north with popular and clerical support, it retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in June 1799 and destroyed the French-backed Parthenopean Republic. Its campaign was marked by massacres, and the repression that followed deeply divided the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/army-of-the-holy-faith.jpg" alt="Army of the Holy Faith" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S_elmo_s_antonio_miracolo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
